# agx: Fix rematerialization spilling phis to unlowered memory pseudo-registers
# https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/45090 state=closed
# ### What does this MR do and why?
<!-- Describe in detail what your merge request does and why. -->

```
agx: Fix rematerialization spilling phis to unlowered memory pseudo-registers

When compiling shaders where register demand exceeds single-wave occupancy
but is within maximum available registers, agx_ra enters the constant
rematerialization path (spilling = false, remat = true). Rematerialization
is intended to avoid scratch memory usage entirely (remat_only = true).

However:
1. In compute_w_entry(), if a phi source was evicted because it was
   rematerializable, it was absent from predecessor W_exit. The spiller's
   heuristic treated this source as "spilled" and evicted the entire phi,
   converting the phi destination into a memory register.
2. In min_algorithm() and insert_coupling_code(), spilling phis created memory
   variables even though remat_only was true. In agx_spill(), the second
   spill_ctx used for coupling code did not even propagate remat_only.
3. In agx_ra(), agx_lower_spill() was gated on `if (spilling)`. Because
   `spilling` was false (only `remat` was true), agx_lower_spill() was skipped
   even though mem_slot_count > 0. The memory moves (mrN) survived to final
   instruction encoding, where mr0 was packed as r0 (the AGX hardware
   control flow nesting counter r0l), causing GPU timeouts and UL1C unmapped
   faults on hardware.

Fix this by:
- In compute_w_entry(), skipping rematerializable sources (ctx->remat[v])
  when deciding whether to spill a phi, since they will be rematerialized
  along the edge rather than loaded from memory.
- Propagating remat_only to the coupling spill_ctx and asserting that phis
  are not spilled when remat_only is set.
- In agx_ra(), lowering memory registers whenever mem_slot_count is non-zero,
  defensively preventing unlowered mrN pseudo-registers from surviving to
  code generation.
- In test-lower-spill, adding the RematPhiDoesNotSpill regression test
  covering diamond CFG with rematerializable phi s
